// <Route path="/step2" element={<StepTwo />} /> — renders fine visually
// User: "I click Continue and the app goes dead silent"

The click unmounts the Continue button, so focus falls back to ___b1___ and no announcement fires — a DOM diff is not a navigation event for AT. The standard remedy: give the new view's h1 the attribute ___b2___ so it is programmatically focusable without joining the Tab order, and call ___b3___ on it when the view commits.

